{"name":"Cedar","hex":"#463430","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cedar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A programming language, adding various features to the earlier language Mesa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cedar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cedrus","blocks":[{"text":"Cedrus is a small genus in the pine family, Pinaceae, consisting of 1-3 species of coniferous trees known in English as cedars. They are native to the mountains of the western Himalayas and the Mediterranean region at high altitudes. The trees grow tall with a cylindrical trunk and a wide leafy crown. The cones are erect; the leaves grow in tufts of 15–45 needle leaves, which can be bright green or blue-green with a waxy coat. When the cones are mature, they disintegrate to release the seeds, which are winged. Both pollen and seeds are wind-dispersed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/View_from_the_Barouk_Forest_1.JPG/330px-View_from_the_Barouk_Forest_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedrus","wikidata":"Q128550"},{"title":"List of plants known as cedar","blocks":[{"text":"Cedar is part of the English common name of many trees and other plants, particularly those of the genus Cedrus."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_plants_known_as_cedar","wikidata":"Q5056949"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Cedrus_deodara_1233_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Cedrus_deodara_1233_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/97/Cedrus_deodara_1233_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Cedrus_deodara_1233_%28cropped%29.jpg